    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Gunnar Henderson** (72.48) anchor the Austin Waves as our premier offensive engines. **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against McGreevy, where his elevated efficiency is driven by a strong platoon advantage and a premium leadoff spot. **Gunnar Henderson**, despite a challenging dynamic platoon split against the lefty Lopez, J, remains an essential start due to his elite park factor and high-leverage order position. Meanwhile, **Coby Mayo** (66.72) is our most efficient mid-tier play, as the combination of a hitter-friendly venue and a positive platoon edge allows him to outperform several higher-pedigree names on the roster.\n\nOur bench strategy was razor-thin today, with **Miguel Vargas** (51.20) serving as the most difficult omission. While **Miguel Vargas** offers solid plate discipline, he was edged out by the superior upside of **Sam Antonacci** (56.74), whose exceptional xwOBA and favorable matchup against Hancock provided a higher projected ceiling for stolen base production\u2014a critical KPI for our team. We are tracking two significant risks: **Kyle Tucker** (50.13) and **Andy Pages** (46.58) face a gauntlet in Sale, whose elite xERA mandates caution. While we are starting them, their floors are compromised, and we must monitor if their production holds steady against such high-tier pitching. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** (59.82) is a value play today; despite hitting lower in the order, his matchup against Snelling is a rare opportunity to exploit a double-digit xERA, making him a sneaky source of SB potential.",
